text:
Fine wine in golden cups costs ten thousand a measure;
rare food on jade plates is worth a fortune.
I set down my cup and cast aside my chopsticks; I cannot eat.
I draw my sword and look around, my heart bewildered.

I would cross the Yellow River, but ice blocks its waters;
I would climb the Taihang Mountains, but snow fills their heights.
At leisure I fish beside a jade-green stream;
then, in a dream, I sail beside the sun.

Hard is the road! So hard!
So many turnings—where is the way?
One day I shall ride the wind and cleave the waves;
raise my cloud-high sail and cross the open sea.
